      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "Lycopene, a highly lipophilic C40 isoprenoid, showed only 0.17% systemic availability in humans after ingestion of tomato paste; this supports low oral bioavailability for large lipophilic isoprenoids.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "In a capsule study, only about 2.6% of a 38-mg lycopene dose was absorbed in humans, reinforcing low F for highly lipophilic isoprenoid molecules.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "Phytoene, a flexible C40 isoprenoid, was estimated to have 58.5% absolute oral bioavailability in humans; this is above the 20% threshold but is less transferable because phytoene is smaller and lacks the quinone head.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C13"],
      "claim": "One 13C-lycopene study reported 23.2% bioavailability for all-trans lycopene, slightly above threshold; however, most other lycopene studies report much lower values, and the result is formulation/label-dependent.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "Hyperforin, a polyprenylated phloroglucinol, was described as having high oral bioavailability in an extract; this is contradictory but limited by smaller size and extract formulation.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low: the query is a CoQ10-like ubiquinone with a polar quinone head and a very long polyprenyl tail; its extreme lipophilicity, high molecular weight, and poor solubility are consistent with the low oral bioavailability seen for tocotrienol and most lycopene studies. The high phytoene and hyperforin records are less transferable and do not outweigh the direct physicochemical liabilities.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability record for CoQ10/ubiquinone is present in the provided evidence.",
    "The high phytoene bioavailability estimate is based on compartmental modeling and may not translate to the larger, quinone-containing query molecule.",
